    <h2 id="consumer-rights">Consumer Rights to List and the Two Request Channels</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Know</strong> what is collected, from where, why, and who receives it (§1798.110), and what was sold, shared, or disclosed (§1798.115).</li>
      <li><strong>Delete</strong> personal information collected from the consumer (§1798.105).</li>
      <li><strong>Correct</strong> inaccurate information (§1798.106).</li>
      <li><strong>Opt out</strong> of sale or sharing (§1798.120).</li>
      <li><strong>Limit</strong> the use of sensitive personal information (§1798.121).</li>
      <li><strong>Non-discrimination</strong> for using these rights (§1798.125).</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Request channels.</strong> Section 1798.130(a)(1)(A) requires two or more methods for requests to know, delete, or correct, including at minimum a toll-free phone number. A business that operates exclusively online and has a direct relationship with the consumer only needs an email address. A business with a website must also accept requests through it (§1798.130(a)(1)(B)).</p>

    <p><strong>Deadlines.</strong> Responses are due within 45 days of a verifiable request, extendable once by 45 days with notice (§1798.130(a)(2)(A)). Opt-out requests need not be verifiable and cannot require an account (11 CCR §7026).</p>

    <h2 id="do-not-sell-or-share">"Do Not Sell or Share" and What Triggers It</h2>

    <p><strong>Selling</strong> (§1798.140(ad)) is disclosing personal information to a third party for money or other valuable consideration. <strong>Sharing</strong> (§1798.140(ah)) is disclosing it for cross-context behavioral advertising, paid or not: targeting ads using data about a person's activity on other businesses' sites and apps (§1798.140(k)). A retargeting pixel sending cookie IDs and page views to an ad network is the standard example. Disclosures to a contracted service provider (§1798.140(ag)) are neither.</p>

    <p>A business that sells or shares must put a clear and conspicuous homepage link titled <strong>"Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information"</strong> (§1798.135(a)). If it uses sensitive personal information beyond the purposes in §1798.121(a), it also needs a <strong>"Limit the Use of My Sensitive Personal Information"</strong> link, or one combined link. The regulations (11 CCR §7025) require it to honor opt-out preference signals such as Global Privacy Control.</p>

    <p>Two more rules: selling or sharing data of consumers known to be under 16 needs opt-in consent, from a parent if the child is under 13 (§1798.120(c)). And a business that sells or shares nothing must say so prominently (§1798.130(a)(5)(C)(i)).</p>

    <h2 id="sample-template">Copy-Ready California Privacy Notice Template</h2>

    <p>Use it standalone or as a section of your main policy. Sections marked <em>[CCPA only]</em> can go if you are below every threshold; sections 6 to 8 cover CalOPPA.</p>

    <div class="copy-block">
      <div class="copy-block-header">
        <span class="copy-block-label">Sample California Privacy Notice — ready to copy</span>
      </div>
      <div class="copy-block-body" id="sample-policy-text">
<p><strong>California Privacy Notice for [Your Business Name]</strong></p>
<p><em>Effective date: [Date] · Last updated: [Date]</em></p>

<p><strong>1. Scope</strong></p>
<p>This notice supplements our Privacy Policy for California residents using [yourwebsite.com].</p>

<p><strong>2. Personal Information We Collect</strong></p>
<p>In the past 12 months we collected the categories below. For each: examples; sources; purposes; recipients; whether sold or shared; retention.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Identifiers:</strong> [name, email, IP address, cookie IDs]; from [you, your browser]; to [respond to inquiries, secure and analyze our site]; disclosed to [hosting, email and analytics providers]; [not sold or shared / shared with advertising partners]; kept [24 months after last contact].</li>
<li><strong>Commercial information:</strong> [purchases, billing address]; from [you]; to [process orders]; disclosed to [payment processor, shipping carrier]; not sold or shared; kept [7 years for tax records].</li>
<li><strong>Internet or network activity:</strong> [pages viewed, clicks]; from [cookies and similar technologies]; for [analytics, advertising]; disclosed to [analytics and advertising providers]; [not sold or shared / shared with advertising partners]; kept [14 months].</li>
<li><strong>Geolocation data:</strong> [approximate location from IP address]; for [analytics, fraud prevention]; disclosed to [analytics provider]; not sold or shared; kept [14 months].</li>
</ul>
<p>[We do not collect sensitive personal information.] / [We use [category] only for purposes permitted by Cal. Civ. Code §1798.121(a).]</p>

<p><strong>3. Sale and Sharing</strong></p>
<p>[We do not sell or share personal information and have not done so in the past 12 months.] / [We share identifiers and internet activity with advertising partners for cross-context behavioral advertising. To opt out, use the "Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information" link on our homepage. We honor Global Privacy Control signals.] We do not sell or share personal information of consumers we know are under 16.</p>

<p><strong>4. Your California Rights</strong> <em>[CCPA only]</em></p>
<p>You may request to know the personal information we collected about you, its sources, our purposes, and who received it; to delete it; to correct it; to opt out of its sale or sharing; and to limit our use of sensitive personal information. We will not discriminate against you for using these rights.</p>

<p><strong>5. How to Submit a Request</strong> <em>[CCPA only]</em></p>
<p>[Call toll-free [1-800-XXX-XXXX]] / [email [privacy@yourwebsite.com]] / [use the form at [URL]]. We verify requests by [method]. An authorized agent may act for you with proof of authority. We respond within 45 days, or tell you if we need 45 more.</p>

<p><strong>6. Reviewing Your Information</strong></p>
<p>[Update your details in [account settings]] / [email [privacy@yourwebsite.com]] to review or change the personal information we hold.</p>

<p><strong>7. Do Not Track and Third-Party Tracking</strong></p>
<p>Our site [does not respond to / responds as follows to: [describe]] browser "Do Not Track" signals. [Third parties such as [providers] may collect information about your activity over time and across websites when you use our site.] / [We do not allow third-party tracking across websites.]</p>

<p><strong>8. Changes</strong></p>
<p>We review this notice at least every 12 months and announce material changes by [updating the date above / emailing registered users].</p>

<p><strong>9. Contact</strong></p>
<p>[Your Business Name] · [privacy@yourwebsite.com] · [Toll-free number, if applicable] · [Business address]</p>
      </div>
      <button class="copy-btn" id="copy-policy-btn" type="button">Copy to clipboard</button>
    </div>

    <p>Prefer answering questions? The <a href="/">free privacy policy generator</a> builds a full policy, and the <a href="/resources/gdpr-privacy-policy-template/">GDPR privacy notice template</a> covers EU visitors.</p>

